WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.892 --> 00:00:18.376
Sign in and open Sales, then Refunds. The page lists every return made so far.

2
00:00:18.476 --> 00:00:24.116
Select New return. You need an open register, because the refund money leaves your till.

3
00:00:24.216 --> 00:00:29.636
Type the sale number from the customer's receipt. Matching sales appear as you type.

4
00:00:29.737 --> 00:00:33.178
Select Find sale to open the return form for it.

5
00:00:33.278 --> 00:00:37.654
Each line shows what was sold and how many can still be returned.

6
00:00:37.754 --> 00:00:43.231
Use plus on a line to set the Return qty. Here one unit comes back, a partial refund.

7
00:00:43.331 --> 00:00:48.312
Set the condition. Resellable puts the item back in stock, Damaged does not.

8
00:00:48.412 --> 00:00:52.387
Pick a reason so your reports show why items come back.

9
00:00:52.487 --> 00:00:56.567
The running total shows exactly how much will be refunded.

10
00:00:56.667 --> 00:01:01.702
Under Refund payout choose how to pay out. Cash comes from the open register.

11
00:01:01.802 --> 00:01:07.609
Select Process return. To return a whole sale, raise every line to its full quantity first.

12
00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:11.261
The receipt now shows the refund against the sale.

13
00:01:11.361 --> 00:01:16.952
Back in Sales, Refunds, every return is listed with its refund number, sale and amount.

14
00:01:18.853 --> 00:01:22.404
Search by refund or sale number to find one again.
